# Overview
runtime=sum(json.loads(p.read_text())['duration'] for p in A.glob('lesson-*-timing.json'))
body=f'<section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">Module 02 · Review candidate</div><h1>{E(D["title"])}</h1><p class="lede">Turn a pharmaceutical project into a clear chain of requirements, risk controls and evidence.</p><p><span class="pill">10 narrated lessons</span><span class="pill">40 explanatory visuals</span><span class="pill">2 interactive explorers</span><span class="pill">Workbook + capstone</span></p><a class="button" href="/academy-lesson-2-1.html">Start Lesson 2.1 →</a></section><div class="grid"><section class="panel"><h2>One project. Connected decisions.</h2><p>Follow fictional mixing vessel V-201 from intended use through programme planning, requirements, risk assessment and handover. Designed for early-career pharmaceutical quality, validation, engineering and production colleagues.</p><p>Prerequisite: <a href="/academy-gmp-foundations.html">Module 1 — GMP Foundations</a>.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Learn at your pace</h2><p>Narration: {runtime/60:.1f} minutes across ten micro-lessons.</p><p>Allow roughly 4–5 hours for a beginner to read, draft answers and review; experienced learners may need less. Activity estimates total 210 minutes, plus about 20 minutes of narration and 30–60 minutes of reading/assessment. These are unmeasured planning estimates, not accredited contact time.</p><p>Use captions, the complete transcript or the illustrated reading path. The videos introduce the topics; required reading and worked examples supply additional assessed content.</p></section></div><section class="panel"><h2>Your self-study progress</h2><p id="progress-text">0 of 10 lessons marked studied · 0 of 10 checks passed</p><progress id="progress-bar" value="0" max="10" aria-label="Lessons marked studied"></progress><p id="assessment-status">Final assessment not completed.</p><p class="muted">Progress stays in memory unless you enable device saving below. It is not a formal training or competency record.</p></section><h2>Course lessons</h2><div class="grid">'
for l in D['lessons']:body+=f'<article class="panel lesson-card"><div class="eyebrow">Lesson 2.{l["id"]}</div><h3>{E(l["title"])}</h3><p>{E(l["objective"])}</p><a href="/academy-lesson-2-{l["id"]}.html">Open lesson 2.{l["id"]} →</a></article>'
body+='</div><section class="panel"><h2>Keep a practical takeaway</h2><p>Prepare an intended-use statement, programme outline, requirement list, traceability matrix, risk assessment and reasoned handover decision. Model answers support self-review.</p><div class="download-list"><a href="/academy-module-2-workbook.html">Open printable workbook</a><a href="/academy-module-2-assessment.html">Take the 20-question assessment</a><a href="/academy-module-2-sources.html">Sources and review information</a></div></section>'
page(D['title'],body,'academy-module-2.html')
# Workbook
body='<div class="eyebrow">Module 02 / Practical workbook</div><h1>Build the evidence chain</h1><p class="lede">Use the fictional V-201 project. Do not enter confidential site, patient or client information.</p><p>Answers remain on this page only and are not stored. Print or save a PDF before closing. Device progress saving does not save workbook answers.</p><button class="no-print" id="print-workbook" type="button">Print / save workbook as PDF</button><p class="notice">Training templates only. These are not approved GMP records. All real acceptance criteria, responsibilities and approvals require the applicable site process.</p><section class="panel"><h2>Project brief</h2><p>V-201 is a jacketed vessel for aqueous oral-solution preparation before filling. Product-contact material records exist. Mixing range, transfer-hose cleaning evidence and alarm-response verification are unresolved. No real product specifications or operating limits are provided.</p><p><a href="/assets/academy/module-2/traceability-template.csv" download>Download traceability worksheet (CSV)</a> · <a href="/assets/academy/module-2/risk-template.csv" download>Download risk worksheet (CSV)</a> · <a href="/assets/academy/module-2/illustrative-data.csv" download>Download fictional data (CSV)</a></p></section>'
for l in D['lessons']:
 i=l['id'];body+=f'<section class="panel" id="activity-{i}"><h2>Activity {i} · {E(l["title"])}</h2><p>Suggested working time: {[15,30,15,25,30,15,25,15,10,30][i-1]} minutes.</p><p>{E(l["activity"])}</p><p>Study the lesson notes and any worked example before drafting your response.</p><label for="work-{i}">Your response to activity {i}</label><textarea id="work-{i}" spellcheck="true"></textarea><details><summary>Model reasoning — compare after writing</summary><p>{E(l["model"])}</p></details><p><a href="/academy-lesson-2-{i}.html">Revisit Lesson 2.{i}</a></p></section>'
body+='<section class="panel"><h2>Capstone self-review rubric</h2><p>Score each dimension 0 (missing), 1 (partly supported), or 2 (clear and supported): intended-use scope; requirement quality; evidence traceability; risk/control rationale; decision and open actions. A maximum of 10 is a learning rubric, not a competency certification.</p><p>A decision that invents missing evidence or approves routine use despite unresolved critical gaps needs correction regardless of total score.</p></section>'
page('Practical workbook',body,'academy-module-2-workbook.html')
extraqs=[
('The URS was revised after DQ approval. Which status is most defensible?',['DQ remains approved without further action if the drawing is unchanged','Document the URS change impact and reassess affected DQ evidence before relying on its status','Repeat PQ immediately without reviewing the design'],1,'A change to user requirements can affect the design qualification basis.'),
('The jacket utility is qualified, but its supply conditions differ from the vessel design assumptions. What is needed?',['Assess interface compatibility and affected verification','Treat utility qualification alone as sufficient for the vessel','Retest the vessel nameplate only'],0,'Qualification of a supplying system does not establish its suitability for every receiving interface.'),
('Draft PB-02 proposes ±0.5 °C but the base project has no approved temperature tolerance. What is URS-02 status?',['Verified because a worked example states a number','Ready for execution because a supplier offers that accuracy','Pending justification and approval of the acceptance basis'],2,'Teaching assumptions cannot replace authorized project requirements.'),
('A supplier FAT passed, but the installed controller firmware differs. Which decision is defensible?',['Accept all FAT results because the hardware matches','Assess the firmware change, applicability of supplier evidence and affected site tests','Reject all supplier evidence regardless of relevance'],1,'Supplier results require documented applicability to the installed configuration.'),
('An FMEA detection score is reduced after an alarm is proposed but not challenged. What is the issue?',['Control effectiveness has not been demonstrated to support the revised score','Documenting the proposed alarm is sufficient evidence','Severity must decrease whenever detection improves'],0,'Residual risk scoring should follow evidence of effectiveness, not an untested proposal.'),
('An independent low-speed detector is proposed for the agitator. Which verification best supports independence?',['Confirm both detectors are listed in the drawing','Verify only the normal speed indication','Challenge primary-sensor failure and verify independent detection and transfer inhibition'],2,'The verification should challenge the common-cause scenario and protective response.'),
('A signed error dataset sums to +3.1 °C across ten readings. What is its signed mean?',['+0.31 °C','+0.50 °C','+0.60 °C'],0,'The signed arithmetic mean is +3.1/10 = +0.31 °C.'),
('With an illustrative absolute limit of 0.5 °C, how many listed errors exceed the limit?',['Zero','One','Two'],1,'Only 0.6 °C exceeds the illustrative limit; 0.5 °C equals it.'),
('A new product changes cleaning needs. Which action is justified?',['Retest mixing only and retain the cleaning basis','Review intended use, requirements, risks and affected verification evidence','Update only the cleaning procedure without assessing interfaces'],1,'New intended use may affect linked requirements and qualification evidence.'),
('What does completing this self-study module demonstrate?',['Formal site authorization','Regulatory certification','Completion of an educational exercise, not independent competence'],2,'Formal competency and authorization require an applicable independently approved process.')
]
questions=[dict(question=q,options=o,answer=a,feedback=f) for q,o,a,f in new_questions]+[dict(question=q,options=o,answer=a,feedback=f) for q,o,a,f in extraqs]
body='<div class="eyebrow">Module 02 / Final self-assessment</div><h1>Test the decisions, not just the terms</h1><p class="lede">20 questions · Suggested practice target: 80% (16/20). Review explanations and retry as needed.</p><p>This is a learning target, not a regulatory threshold or formal competency assessment. Unanswered questions must be completed before scoring. Responses are not sent to a server. This is an open-book self-study exercise: answers and explanations are visible in the page source and downloadable key. Scores do not demonstrate independent competence. Read the lesson notes and required extensions where provided before attempting it.</p><form class="quiz" data-final="true">'+''.join(quiz(q,i) for i,q in enumerate(questions,1))+'<button type="submit" disabled>Score assessment</button><p class="quiz-result" role="status" tabindex="-1"></p></form><p><a href="/academy-module-2-workbook.html#activity-10">Complete the capstone</a> · <a href="/academy-module-2.html">Return to overview</a></p><noscript><p>Interactive scoring requires JavaScript. Use the printable answer key linked below.</p></noscript><details><summary>Printable answer key and explanations</summary>'+''.join(f'<p>{i}. {E(q["options"][q["answer"]])} — {E(q["feedback"])}</p>' for i,q in enumerate(questions,1))+'</details>'
page('Final self-assessment',body,'academy-module-2-assessment.html')
