body='<div class="eyebrow">Module 02 / Reference and review notes</div><h1>Sources, examples and provenance</h1><section class="panel"><h2>Technical basis</h2><p>Rechecked against official sources on 27 October 2026. This module focuses on human-medicinal-product qualification planning using EU GMP and ICH principles, with WHO validation guidance as supplementary context. It does not claim complete Indian, US, veterinary or product-specific compliance coverage.</p>'+source_links()+'<p>The European Commission listing still identifies the 2015 Annex 15 as the operative text. The EMA 2026 Annex 15 concept-paper consultation is closed; its July corrigendum updates the revision timetable, not the operative GMP text. Revision proposals are not taught as adopted requirements. The EMA listing identifies Q9(R1) as effective from 26 July 2023, with the current corrected publication listed in 2025.</p><p><a href="https://health.ec.europa.eu/medicinal-products/eudralex/eudralex-volume-4_en">Official EU GMP index</a> · <a href="https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/scientific-guidelines/ich-q9-quality-risk-management">EMA Q9 status</a></p></section><section class="panel"><h2>How to distinguish the material</h2><p>Regulatory principles are linked to the sources above. V-201, document IDs, responsibilities, diagrams, questions and the dataset are original fictional teaching examples. The three-level score, 0.5 °C example limit and 80% quiz target are not regulatory acceptance criteria.</p><p>The recorded narration is transcribed with conventional written abbreviations and numerals on each lesson page. Required reading adds assessed material that is not in the recordings. Activities and model reasoning are explicitly separate extensions. Diagrams have nearby text labels, explanatory narration and full-size versions; the data chart has an exact-value table.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Media and rights record</h2><p>All forty diagrams were drawn specifically for this module using reproducible source code. No stock pharmaceutical photographs, third-party logos, client data, music or identifiable people are used. Narration uses the existing Kokoro stock af_heart voice, not a cloned person. Model and voice files are from the existing project toolchain; applicable Apache 2.0 model and MIT runtime notices are retained in the repository rights record. Diagram text uses DejaVu Sans, with its <a href="/assets/academy/dejavu-font-notice.txt">DejaVu font notice retained here</a>. This provenance record is not a legal clearance opinion.</p><p>Lesson video, captions, diagrams and scripts are served from this site. No external video embeds, analytics or advertising scripts are added by Module 2. This describes application code only: Cloudflare account settings, edge logging, analytics, retention and deletion controls have not been independently verified.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Privacy and device storage</h2><p>Pressing Play requests the lesson video from the site host. Page, image and caption requests may occur when you open a lesson. The host can receive your IP address and ordinary request metadata; hosting retention and account terms are governed by the site operator. Module 2 does not collect names or send quiz responses or workbook answers to a server.</p><p>Optional localStorage uses the key valistera_module2_v1 for your preference, lesson-study markers, quiz passes and final score. Workbook text is never saved by this module. Clear Module 2 saved progress removes that key and disables saving. Private browsing, storage blocking or clearing site data may remove progress. On shared devices, clear progress when finished. See the <a href="/privacy.html">website privacy policy</a>.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Review status</h2><p><a href="/academy-module-2-review.html">Open the accessible review package and finding responses</a></p><p>Prepared for consultant review; not published to production and not approved for regulated use. Human listening, real-device comfort, assistive-technology acceptance and independent technical approval must not be inferred from automated tests. Review findings should identify the lesson, scene or timestamp and proposed correction.</p></section>'
page('Sources and review notes',body,'academy-module-2-sources.html')
print('Built 14 HTML pages and learning resources')

